.TH AGORYX 1 "2026-10-05" "Agoryx 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agoryx \- a local-first workspace for you and your AI agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agoryx up
.RI "[-d] [--port N]"
.br
.B agoryx open
.RI "[room]"
.br
.B agoryx new
.RI "[name] [--mode chat|work] [--dir folder] [--worktree] [-m message]"
.br
.B agoryx say
.RI "[-r room] text"
.br
.B agoryx help rooms
.br
.B agoryx doctor
.RI "[--probe] [--json]"
.br
.B agoryx service
.RI "install|uninstall|status [--json]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Agoryx brings a human and native Claude Code/Codex agents into shared
conversations.
The web UI, macOS shell and room CLI share a local JSONL event runtime.
Projects group conversations independently of their mode and execution folder.
.PP
Chat and Work use shared native sessions. Verification, Council, Tournament
and Debate
have separate private phases, atomic reveal and mode-specific results.
Start these protocols in the web or desktop UI. Private execution requires the
supported
macOS Seatbelt backend and refuses to run without that boundary.
.PP
Local-first describes storage and coordination. Model prompts still go to the
selected
provider through its native CLI. The desktop distribution requires Apple
Silicon,
Node.js 22 or newer, and signed-in native agent CLIs.
.SH ROOM COMMANDS
.TP
.B up / down / open
Start or stop the daemon, or open its authenticated web UI. The default port
is 7717.
The daemon listens on loopback unless LAN or trusted proxy access is
explicitly enabled.
.TP
.B new / rooms
Create a Chat or Work conversation, or list conversations.
.TP
.B say / tail / more / stop
Post a message, inspect or follow the conversation, request another round, or
stop execution.
.TP
.B table
Inspect or act on the room's questions, proposals, evidence, decisions and
components.
.TP
.B project / memory
Inspect or explicitly update the conversation's project and its event-backed
memory.
Use --dir to address a project folder directly.
.TP
.B doc / diff / revert
Inspect the canonical document, per-turn changes and recovery snapshots.
Reverting files does not rewind conversation or table history.
.TP
.B resume
Print the native Claude/Codex session resume commands.
.TP
.B pair / devices
Pair a phone using an expiring code, list paired devices or revoke access.
.PP
Run "agoryx help rooms" for the complete grammar and flags.
.SH INSTALLATION AND DIAGNOSTICS
.TP
.B doctor
Check Node, the build, native SQLite loading, agent installations/sign-ins,
Git,
state access and daemon status. --json prints structured results.
--probe additionally sends a short real prompt to each signed-in provider.
.TP
.B service
On macOS, install, uninstall or inspect a per-user launchd daemon service.
Install it again after moving the installation or changing Node.
.SH LEGACY TERMINAL CHAT
Running agoryx without a subcommand, or running "agoryx chat", starts the
older
SQLite terminal runtime. It is separate from Rooms.
Its policies are free, manual, round-robin, auto and team.
Use "agoryx chat --help" for flags and "/help" inside a session.
The sessions and config commands operate on this compatibility runtime.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $AGORYX_HOME
Override for room, project, workflow and daemon state.
The default is $XDG_STATE_HOME/agoryx/agora, falling back to
~/.local/state/agoryx/agora.
.TP
.I $AGORYX_WORKSPACES
Override for new Work folders. With a custom AGORYX_HOME, the default is its
workspaces
subdirectory; otherwise it is ~/agoryx.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/agoryx/config.json
Legacy terminal configuration; falls back to ~/.config/agoryx/config.json.
A local agoryx.json is also recognized by that runtime.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/agoryx/agoryx.db
Legacy SQLite database; falls back to ~/.local/state/agoryx/agoryx.db.
